WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:01.049
OK.

00:00:01.049 --> 00:00:03.350
This is a huge deal, so we're going to spend
some time on this.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.740
Donald Trump admitted during one of his weekend
press briefings from his club in Bedminster,

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:13.260
New Jersey, where he gathered a crowd of supporters
to cheer for him during a press briefing and

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.260
to boo reporters.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.850
I mean, this is complete.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.070
The country is backwards right now.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.070
OK.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:25.829
He said he is going to be permanently cutting
funding to Social Security and Medicare.

00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:27.400
How did he say it?

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.400
Take a look.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.550
Because it might not be obvious if I'm victorious
on November 3rd.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.239
I plan to forgive these taxes and make permanent
cuts to the payroll tax.

00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:37.890
I'm going to make them all permanent.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:38.969
Wait a second.

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:41.789
Did he say Social Security there?

00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:43.530
What is this about Social Security?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.850
Let me explain it to you.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:49.989
Donald Trump is finally admitting here that
if he is reelected, he will permanently cut

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:54.920
the employee side of the Social Security deduction
from wages.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.250
This is how Social Security is funded.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.230
This is a huge red alert.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:02.379
This is not getting the attention it deserves.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:07.840
And what's crazy is you still have some people,
including people on the left, saying Biden

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.330
will cut your Social Security if he's president.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:15.920
Not something Biden has even talked about
for 27 years, since 1993, during which he

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.180
said he wouldn't preemptively take it off
the table.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:25.330
This is Donald Trump saying, I am going to
permanently reduce the money that is the primary

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:27.550
funding source for Social Security.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.920
So let's talk it through earlier in the pandemic.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.060
Donald Trump started talking

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:36.640
about waiving the so-called payroll tax for
employees through the end of the year.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.340
That tax is shared between you and your employer.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.440
If you are self-employed, you pay all of it.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:49.970
But for most people, there are W-2 employee,
for example, like producer Pat Pat pays seven

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:53.030
point six five percent out of his salary.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:56.230
And then I put in another seven point six
five percent.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:59.380
For him, it's a total of fifteen point three
percent.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.400
It's mostly Social Security and a little bit
for Medicare.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.470
That's how we fund Social Security.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:11.290
So Trump floats the idea, hey, pandemic economics
or disaster?

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:16.790
Let's put more money in people's pockets by
cutting the seven point six five percent paid

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:17.860
by the employee.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:22.200
Immediately, the employees get to keep another
seven point six five percent from every paycheck.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.200
Great.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.220
But the way that it was originally conceived
was a deferral, meaning

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:31.340
you get that money in your paycheck through
the end of the year.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.569
But when you file your taxes in 2021 for 2020,
you owe that back.

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:37.990
It was just a deferral.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.350
It gets added back in wasn't even permanent.

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:43.880
It's a temporary savings and then you get
a bill for it.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.300
Now, Trump is again going for the payroll
tax idea.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:51.420
He's looking at it via executive order, which
he said when Barack Obama was president is

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.410
being overused, that he wouldn't do things
through executive order, he'd do them through

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:58.390
legislation, except he's not doing it.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.950
But except he says he'll give you the payroll
tax deferral for now.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:08.050
If he's reelected, he will forgive the repayment
of the payroll tax.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.860
We think I mean, it's so convoluted that even
Trump has gone back and forth on some of these

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:12.860
points.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:18.370
But now, again, he says in the future, if
he's reelected, he will just cut the employee

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.250
side altogether.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.050
Here he is saying it again.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:26.810
If I'm victorious on November 3rd, I plan
to forgive these taxes and make permanent

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.810
cuts to the payroll tax.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.200
I'm going to make them all permanent.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:35.599
I plan to forgive these taxes and make permanent
cuts.

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:40.930
This is a shadow plan to cut Social Security
and Medicare.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.459
This is a red alert.

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:46.410
Republicans already say Social Security's
in trouble.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.410
It's underfunded.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.250
It won't be able to pay benefits.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.989
What do you think happens if you cut the money
going in?

00:03:52.989 --> 00:03:55.230
You obviously will have to cut the benefits.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:04:00.890
So now we have a dramatically different proposal
from Donald Trump versus Joe Biden on Social

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:01.890
Security.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:07.920
Trump wants permanent cuts to Social Security
taxes, meaning he will have to lower Social

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:08.920
Security benefits.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:12.490
He's looking to neuter Social Security, a
fabric of our country.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:15.780
Really, it's I mean, you know, other countries
have much stronger social safety nets.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.729
One of the things we have, one of the few
things is Social Security.

00:04:19.729 --> 00:04:21.680
Trump wants to neuter it.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:27.830
Biden wants to uncap Social Security taxes
above 400000 dollars.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:33.910
Normally, you only pay payroll tax on the
first hundred and thirty thousand or so of

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:34.910
earnings.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:40.469
That means if you normally earn a million
dollars, you only paid the Social Security

00:04:40.469 --> 00:04:44.729
tax on the first hundred and thirty K above
that, you pay zero.

00:04:44.729 --> 00:04:48.650
Biden's idea is you pay on the first hundred
and thirty.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:52.270
There's then like a donut hole between 130
and 400.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.530
But starting at 400000.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.120
A year in income uncapped.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.130
You pay that seven point six, five percent.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:06.990
That's a huge increase in funding for Social
Security versus Donald Trump, saying he will

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.729
permanently defund it.

00:05:09.729 --> 00:05:14.650
This is a topic which is not getting huge
airtime right now.

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:17.259
And we need to force it to get more attention.

00:05:17.259 --> 00:05:21.970
Hopefully, it will be a big part of the debates
between Trump and Biden if they happen, because

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.860
it is of such huge significance to the vast
majority of the United States.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:26.860
Just think back.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:32.110
Trump was supposedly the economic populist,
big populism, wonderful populism from Donald

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:33.110
Trump.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:38.539
He is now saying if you reelect him, he will
neuter permanently Social Security.

00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:42.539
And you can take to the bank the realization
that shortly thereafter they're are going

00:05:42.539 --> 00:05:45.029
to say, hey, we gave you the payroll tax.

00:05:45.029 --> 00:05:46.070
People are getting the money out front.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.990
But we're going to have to cut Social Security
benefits as a result.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:53.129
We're no longer funding it to the extent that
we previously were.

00:05:53.129 --> 00:05:54.800
Don't allow this issue to be ignored.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.729
Democrats need to run hard with this all the
way to November.

00:05:58.729 --> 00:06:03.879
And you know that Republicans would do the
exact same thing if Democrats suggested even

00:06:03.879 --> 00:06:07.669
smaller changes to programs they believe are
important.

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:12.800
This is an attempt at a massive destruction
of one of the most important programs that

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:18.349
exists in the United States to even maintain
financial solvency for so many millions of

00:06:18.349 --> 00:06:20.049
Americans once they hit retirement

